  "summary": "Deterministic evaluation under Node 26.5.0: 0/7 hard gates failing and 0/4 quality targets open. The knowledge-lifecycle suite passed 50/50 tests; knowledge-bank and public-safety checks passed with 10 careful-claim guardrail warnings. Weighted judge result: 100.0/100, with all seven criteria at 4/4. The new @wowlist census reconciles all 38 items in the observed surviving-profile control as 16 account posts, six account replies, and 16 reposts from 13 public accounts, while explicitly refusing native-export or deletion-history language. Its Chad-lens origin-and-support claim turns all six replies into a concrete product-support and onboarding result, credits Jamie and Richard collectively, leaves individual shared-account authorship unassigned, and remains deferred from website projection. Current visible reactions are dated and separated from repost-source metrics, adoption, endorsement, audience, and impact; linked articles are retained as mission context rather than WOW List press coverage. Mature population, network, scene-knowledge, civic-care, and reaction findings remain reserve knowledge rather than automatic website copy. The public ledger preserves 38 unique item records and SHA-256 content digests while omitting raw post text and authenticated-session material. Remaining bounded limits are that the census cannot establish deleted earlier items, individual post authorship, complete support workload, historical analytics, unique people, adoption, endorsement, or causal impact; account-establishment and private recording evidence still require research and collaborator review; the strengthened claim still requires human editorial selection; and all three human gates remain pending."
